[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="MKConfig" load_steps=35 format=3]

; The demo's own config. Everything that needs host provisioning lives here rather than in the
; addon, which is what keeps the shipped defaults cold-droppable into an empty project.
;
; The Credits page is the shipped proof of the host-added-page path: its scene and its page def are
; both in demo/, and no addon file references either.
;
; This is also where the backend slots get real parameters. MKSceneMenuBackend names no scene of its
; own — the addon may not reference demo/ — so the demo supplies game_scene and menu_scene through
; its slot's params, which is the mechanism that exists so a host never has to subclass a backend to
; change one value. The network slot points at MKStubNetworkBackend here, while the shipped default
; config leaves it empty: the demo is where the server browser is meant to be visible.
;
; Phase 5 wires the character flow, and the demo takes the OPPOSITE side of every default the addon
; ships — which is the only way both sides get exercised:
;
;   - creation_steps is AUTHORED here, all four in order. The addon leaves it empty and
;     MKCharacterCreate falls back to its built-in Name -> Archetype -> Appearance order; authoring it
;     is what proves the explicit-ordering path, and it is the only way to reach the fourth step.
;   - point_buy_schema is ASSIGNED (demo/demo_creation/pointbuy_schema.tres). D17 ships point-buy off,
;     so the demo turns it on: a disabled-by-default feature nobody can see is a feature nobody tests.
;     The pointbuy step def below is why the two go together — with a null schema the host DROPS that
;     step with a debug line, so authoring the step without the schema would silently give three.
;   - archetypes are the three real ones in demo/demo_archetypes/, replacing the addon's single
;     neutral "Traveler" placeholder. They are standalone .tres files, not sub-resources, because
;     unlike the placeholder they ARE meant to be read and copied by a host authoring its own.
;
; character_create is hidden (visible = false), the same mechanism the "sub" page below uses: off the
; nav bar, reachable by id, which is what MKCharacterSelect's push_page needs. Reaching a half-built
; character by clicking a nav tab — and losing it by clicking another — is what the back-stack ladder
; exists to prevent.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://addons/menu_kit/core/mk_config.gd" id="1_config"]
